{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-316324",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The equation of the regression line is given by\n\n$$\ny=mx+b,\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{S}_{xy}}{{S}_{xx}},\\,b=\\overset{―}{y}-m\\overset{―}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's compute $m:$\n\n- First, we compute the sum in the numerator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xy} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =(1-3)(8-4)+(2-3)(6-4) \\\\  & +(4-3)(2-4)+(5-3)(0-4) \\\\  & =(-2)(4)+(-1)(2)+(1)(-2)+(2)(-4) \\\\  & =-8-2-2-8 \\\\  & =-20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Second, we compute the sum in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xx} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =(1-3)^{2}+(2-3)^{2}+(4-3)^{2}+(5-3)^{2} \\\\  & =4+1+1+4 \\\\  & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting into the formula for $m,$ we obtain \n\n$$\nm=\\frac{-20}{10}=-2.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute into the formula for $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =\\overset{―}{y}-m\\overset{―}{x} \\\\  & =4-(-2)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =4+6 \\\\  & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the regression line is\n\n$$\ny=-2x+10.\n$$",
